  "trusted_and_scoped_premises": [
    "Hasher::write, write_usize, and the to_ne_bytes observers are external std contracts. The Hash model records mutable Hasher invariant preservation only.",
    "The default write_isize body is source-shaped and proved; it calls write_usize once with isize_to_usize_word(value). The helper postcondition proves the unsigned logical value is value for nonnegative inputs and usize::MAX + 1 + value for negative inputs. Boundary-value runtime test compares the same helper implementation to Rust casts.",
    "The logical conversion formula is word-width-parametric via usize::MAX; it does not specify hash output bytes. Exact digest semantics remain outside the model.",
    "The generic NonZero<T> forwarding spec requires NonZeroPrimitiveModel for model resolution. Current modeled applicability is only the primitive subset represented by that relation, including u16.",
    "These are proved external-spec wrapper/helper bodies under the listed callback and observer contracts, not source-included proofs of core/alloc implementations.",
    "No Hash/Eq coherence property or hash digest is specified or proved."
  ],
  "result_classification": "Fresh source-matched std proof; HTTP consumers must be re-emitted and reproved against these final contracts before claiming integrated Hash closure."
